# Distribution for CommonsBase_Dk (Linux x86_64 musl)

Ships the fully static musl `dk0` and `dk1` executables for musl distros
such as alpine (a static musl binary also runs on every glibc distro). The
closure builds on the same glibc manylinux container as `Linux_x86_64`; the
`Release.Linux_x86_64_musl` slot's DkML toolchain (a pinned x86_64-linux-musl
cross gcc) and its `LDFLAGS=-static` default do the rest.

The value-ids below are harvested from the first CI run (the DkML pattern).

## Dk0 executable

  $ get-object CommonsBase_Dk.Dk0@2.4.2 -s Release.Linux_x86_64_musl -m ./bin/dk0.exe -f ${RUNTIME}/Linux_x86_64_musl-dk0.exe
  \test(pass)
  \dk.object(abi: "Release.Linux_x86_64_musl", value-id: "oqgmnirgqspcstizwvtw7sssu3lnae46kud6tkoafwshfaadkygwa")\;

## Dk1 executable

  $ get-object CommonsBase_Dk.Dk1@2.4.2 -s Release.Linux_x86_64_musl -m ./bin/dk1.exe -f ${RUNTIME}/Linux_x86_64_musl-dk1.exe
  \test(pass)
  \dk.object(abi: "Release.Linux_x86_64_musl", value-id: "o3hh7ymm3un4i77njsgohdh4u73wkbmutla7qhtm32gqnlr4a2msq")\;
